{"data_type": "permanent_rule", "name": "On a phone with Pro/manual video, lock white balance to a Kelvin value for talking-head videos (about 5600K for daylight, 3200K for warm bulbs) -- auto white balance can shift skin tone mid-video as hands or a screen change colour. On an auto-only phone, use one light source so auto white balance has nothing to chase.", "en": "Locked white balance", "hi": "White balance lock karo"}
{"data_type": "permanent_rule", "name": "In video, stay on the phone's optical lenses (the 0.5x ultrawide, the 1x, and the 2x/3x/3.5x telephoto if the phone has them) and never zoom digitally past them -- move the phone closer instead; digital zoom throws away detail.", "en": "Real lenses, no digital zoom", "hi": "Asli lens, digital zoom nahi"}
{"data_type": "permanent_rule", "name": "Always wipe the camera lens with a microfiber cloth before recording — micro-scratches and finger oil cause severe highlight halation, worsened by humidity and dust common in Indian outdoor environments.", "en": "Clean lens first", "hi": "Pehle lens saaf karo"}
